%description:

A radio link has one realization, and both of its ends should see it.

That is the premise LinkKey is built on: the key is normalized so that a link
is the same key from either end (ChannelModelBase.h), and the per-link
shadowing, LOS and fading state is indexed by it. Reciprocity is what makes
that worth doing.

Without shadowing the two directions agree exactly. The downlink and uplink
budgets differ only by constants -- the two transmit powers and the two noise
figures, since the antenna gains and the cable loss appear in both -- so

    SINR_DL - SINR_UL = (eNodeBTxPower - ueTxPower) - (ueNoiseFigure - bsNoiseFigure)

which the model reproduces to the last digit. That check is worth having on
its own: it is the only assertion in this directory on the uplink budget, and
it says that both directions traverse the same path loss.

With shadowing the same difference has to stay the same constant, because
shadowing is a property of the link and not of the direction of travel. It
does not. computeShadowing reads two different maps depending on which
direction it is serving: a downlink CQI takes the map stored on the UE
(obtainShadowingMap), everything else takes the evaluating module's own
lastComputedSF_. The key into those maps is the same LinkKey; the maps are
not the same map. So one physical link acquires two independent shadowing
realizations, and measured here the downlink is faded by 2.72 dB while the
uplink is lifted by 9.22 dB at the same instant, for the same pair of nodes,
at the same distance.

Recorded as an expected failure rather than fixed. Which of the two maps
should survive -- or whether both should be replaced by state the medium owns
once per link -- is the same modelling question that decides the data layout
of any refactoring of the medium, and it is not this test's to answer. What
the test is for is that the answer stops being a matter of belief.

%expected-failure: shadowing is drawn per direction, so a link is not reciprocal

%extraargs: -c LinkReciprocity

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config LinkReciprocity]
output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 5s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
seed-set = 0
**.vector-recording = false
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.measuredSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[0].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[0].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 500m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

**.scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = ${shad = false, true}
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
**.ueTxPower = 26dBm
**.antennGainEnB = 18dBi
**.antennaGainUe = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
**.ueNoiseFigure = 7dBm
**.bsNoiseFigure = 5dBm

*.ue[*].numApps = 2
*.server.numApps = 2
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.ue[*].app[1].typename = "CbrSender"
*.ue[*].app[1].destAddress = "server"
*.ue[*].app[1].destPort = 4000
*.ue[*].app[1].localPort = 4088
*.ue[*].app[1].packetSize = 40B
*.ue[*].app[1].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.ue[*].app[1].startTime = 0.1s
*.server.app[1].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.server.app[1].localPort = 4000
*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=2 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
